<Base title="About" reading description="What Rulebook is, what it is not, and who runs it.">
<div class="wrap hero prose"><span class="label eyebrow">About</span><h1>A plain account of what this is.</h1></div>
<div class="wrap prose"><h2>What it is</h2><p>Rulebook is an educational website about investing with discipline. It publishes four rules-based screens, runs a paper-trading terminal that holds you to limits you set while calm, helps you write a one-page investment plan, and keeps a public record of every simulated pick, trade and void.</p>
<h2 data-u="mt6">What it is not</h2><ul><li><strong>Not investment advice.</strong> Nothing here is a recommendation to buy, sell or hold. A screen's list is the output of fixed rules.</li><li><strong>Not a broker.</strong> There is no real-money trading and no broker connection.</li><li><strong>Not a tip service.</strong> There are no calls, targets or alerts about price moves.</li><li><strong>Not a promise.</strong> Every figure is simulated — not real returns. Past simulated results say little about the future, and a short record says even less.</li></ul>
<h2 data-u="mt6">Who runs it</h2><p>Rulebook is built and run by the individual behind askakshay.com, as one of a family of tools. It does not present itself as a SEBI-registered investment adviser or research analyst. If you want advice about your money, speak to a registered adviser.</p>
<h2 data-u="mt6">Why the Gate exists</h2><p>SEBI's own study found that 93% of individual equity derivatives (F&amp;O) traders lost money in FY22–FY24. The Gate does not make trading safe. It makes the habits that lose money harder to repeat, on paper, before real money is involved.</p>
<h2 data-u="mt6">Your data</h2><p>Your Gate trades and Plan stay in your own browser. They are not sent to us and cannot be seen by us. Clearing your browser data removes them, so use the export button. The email list stores your address, the date and the consent text you agreed to. To be removed, reply to any note you receive. We use no tracking pixels.</p>
<h2 data-u="mt6">Limits of the lock</h2><p>The Gate's lock and strict mode are self-commitment tools that live in your browser. Clearing site data or using another device bypasses them. They are there to slow you down, not to stop a determined you.</p>
<h2 data-u="mt6">Data</h2><p>Prices and financial statements come from Yahoo Finance, an unofficial source. It can be wrong or late. Where data is missing, the site says so rather than guessing.</p></div></Base>
